# Update slides with every code change

Whenever you change product behavior, algorithms, event taxonomy, UI structure, APIs, thresholds, or demo flow in this repo, you **must also update** `web/presentation/index.html` in the same turn so slides stay accurate.

## What to sync

- Event types and alert levels (currently only: FALL, STANDING, SQUAT, STOOP, PARTIAL)
- Classifier / fall / PARTIAL rules and confirm timings
- Pipeline steps and architecture (SOC dashboard, not old 3-tab UI)
- IQA: panel badges only — no CAMERA / OFFLINE events
- Deploy/test counts, demo checklist, removed features (MANDOWN, RECOVERED, POSTURE, ERGO, ZONE, PPE, CAMERA, OFFLINE)

## Conventions

- Slides stay in Vietnamese for the audience.
- Code identifiers stay English; do not put Vietnamese into variable/key names in slides' code samples when showing identifiers.
- Do not leave outdated names (IMPROPER, PROPER_LIFT, NONE, MANDOWN, “3 tab Giám sát”, etc.).

## Checklist before finishing

1. Grep slides for removed event/UI names.
2. Align numbers (pytest count, confirm seconds) with code/tests.
3. Mention slide update briefly in the final reply to the user.
